      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-candidate-source.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-14: \"There are other tools for translations that could be used in this workflow\" — the candidate-producing engines as interchangeable Tools behind one interface (a translation-candidate-source kind, if the typology allows). The Tool schema has no kind field; interchangeability is derived from a shared skill and an identical I/O signature, so the interface is this skill. Coordinated 2026-11-14 with the session building `translation:candidates` (cat-harness-tools#2144, cat-harness#1329): the open machine-translation engines are ONE Tool selected by `--engine`, not a node per engine; the agent model is a separate Tool.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/translation-candidate-source.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rules every engine keeps",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-14: candidates are never a barrier to having a translation; a writer that adds candidates for an empty msgstr also writes the first candidate as its msgstr, marked fuzzy (stated in cat-harness-tools scripts/lib/translation-adjudication.ts, CANDIDATES_SCHEMA).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-14"
      ]
    }
  ]
